    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nConsolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey`.\n\n**The key** \u2014 `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.util.OwnerIdentities.identityKey(owner)`:\n```\nnormalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + (householdId or empty)\n```\nEach component is normalized identically for every owner (telephone \u2192 E.164 via the now-`public` `OwnerTelephone.toE164`, email trimmed/lower-cased, blank household/email \u2192 `\"\"`), so comparison is stable and idempotent.\n\n**The check** \u2014 new `CheckUniqueIdentity` function rejects with `DuplicateIdentityException` (409) only when a new owner's *whole* `identityKey` equals an existing owner's. It runs **after** `BuildOwner` and `AssignHousehold` in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, so the new owner's `householdId` is already assigned and part of the key. Because telephone is in the key, two members of the same household with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed \u2014 exactly the behaviour change the spec requires.\n\n**Returned** \u2014 added `identityKey` (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; the `OwnerMapper` populates it via `OwnerIdentities.identityKey(owner)`, so every owner response now carries it.\n\n**Removed** \u2014 the three old check functions (`CheckUniqueTelephone/Household/Email`), their exceptions/handlers, and escalation YAMLs; added the new `DuplicateIdentityException` + handler + escalation YAML. Fixed dangling javadoc `{@link}`s and updated the now-inaccurate `sharesHousehold` description (it now only controls household joining, not the 409 gate).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` (two owners sharing a telephone, nothing else \u2192 same full key \u2192 409) passes.",
